     8	/-!
     9	# Solution: proofs of `TheoremA` and `TheoremA_charP`
    10	
    11	Follows the proof of Theorem 6.5 of the source paper (degree bookkeeping):
    12	
    13	* `JC72108.coeff_bracket` (Step 1): for `natDegree A ≤ a`, `natDegree D ≤ d`
    14	  and `a + d = n + 1`, the coefficient of `y^n` in `A·D′ − ν·A′·D` is
    15	  `(d − ν·a)·(A_a·D_d)`; in particular nothing of higher degree occurs.
    16	* `JC72108.core` (Steps 2–4): the shared rigidity argument over an integral
    17	  domain, with the characteristic packaged as one cast-injectivity hypothesis.
    18	  Step 2 forces `deg C = ν·deg A`; Steps 3–4 subtract the kernel element
    19	  `A^ν` (denominators cleared: `D := lc(A)^ν·C − lc(C)·A^ν`) and read the
    20	  top coefficient once more.
    21	* `TheoremA`, `TheoremA_charP`: the two instantiations (characteristic zero,
    22	  and characteristic `p` with `ν·deg A < p`, `deg C < p`).
    23	-/
    24	
    25	namespace JC72108
    26	
    27	open Polynomial
    28	
   170	    have hDdeg : D.natDegree = (ν' + 1) * A.natDegree :=
   171	      hcast _ hd.le (by push_cast at h0 ⊢; linear_combination h0)
   172	    exact absurd (hDdeg.trans hstep2.symm) hd.ne
   173	
   174	end JC72108
   175	
   176	/-- **Theorem A** (ODE rigidity, all weights; characteristic zero).
   177	If polynomials `A, C` over an integral domain `F` of characteristic zero
   178	satisfy `A·C′ − ν·A′·C = c` with integer weight `ν ≥ 1` and `c` a nonzero
   179	constant, then `deg A ≤ 1`.  (Theorem 6.5 of the source paper.) -/
   180	theorem TheoremA {F : Type*} [CommRing F] [IsDomain F] [CharZero F]
   181	    (ν : ℕ) (hν : 1 ≤ ν) (A C : Polynomial F) (c : F) (hc : c ≠ 0)
   182	    (hode : A * Polynomial.derivative C
   183	        - (ν : Polynomial F) * (Polynomial.derivative A * C) = Polynomial.C c) :
   184	    A.natDegree ≤ 1 :=
   185	  JC72108.core ν hν A C c hc hode fun _ _ h => Nat.cast_injective h
   186	
   187	/-- **Theorem A, positive characteristic.**  Over an integral domain of
   188	characteristic `p`, the same rigidity holds provided `p` dominates the degree
   189	data: `ν·deg A < p` and `deg C < p`.  (Recorded in §6 of the source paper via
   190	the conservative bound `p > (k+1)·d₂`, which implies both hypotheses in the
   191	application there.) -/
   192	theorem TheoremA_charP {F : Type*} [CommRing F] [IsDomain F] (p : ℕ) [CharP F p]
   193	    (ν : ℕ) (hν : 1 ≤ ν) (A C : Polynomial F) (c : F) (hc : c ≠ 0)
   194	    (hνA : ν * A.natDegree < p) (hC : C.natDegree < p)
   195	    (hode : A * Polynomial.derivative C
   196	        - (ν : Polynomial F) * (Polynomial.derivative A * C) = Polynomial.C c) :
   197	    A.natDegree ≤ 1 :=
   198	  JC72108.core ν hν A C c hc hode fun _ hm h =>
   199	    CharP.natCast_injOn_Iio F p (lt_of_le_of_lt hm hC) hνA h
